{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"d450a87d931b1639d18d3607323e740fc4097dbfb3a5747a3035500c27afffa5","slug":"about.get-involved.working-groups","location":"/about/get-involved/working-groups.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Working Groups","github":"https://github.com/UC-OSPO-Network/ucospo.net","copyright":"2024","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/UC-OSPO-Network/ucospo.net/blob/main/about/get-involved/working-groups.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/UC-OSPO-Network/ucospo.net/edit/main/about/get-involved/working-groups.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"working-groups.md","url":"/build/working-groups-b93c3431a3aa4ce7644c1f11afc60d75.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"comment","value":" NOTE 2026-06-16: For now, all Working Groups accept new members and joining the WG's Slack channel is all that's required (the text below reflects this). The longer-term membership/onboarding model is to be designed with Virginia Scarlett in July—the governance doc says each WG sets its own membership criteria, subject to Stewardship Group approval. See task \"Brainstorm Working Group membership openness with Virginia\". ","key":"gXSWzgIZfe"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Working Groups are where most of the Network’s work actually happens. Each one sets its own focus, membership, and way of working, and new groups can form of their own accord when there’s energy for something new. Every Member Organization commits to taking part in at least one. While each group decides who can join, all of the Network’s existing Working Groups are currently open to anyone interested—whether or not your institution has an OSPO or any plans to start one.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"rFyWZ1EeQ9"}],"key":"vKvKJmoOsR"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread